# =========================
# Reference voices (voice cloning) — MUST come after the *.wav rules above
# =========================
# `voices/` holds the reference recordings a character is cloned from. New
# recordings are NOT committed (decided 10/10/2026): in production the private
# S3 voice bucket is the source of truth, and scripts/upload_characters_to_s3.py
# uploads from this folder, so a recording only has to be on disk here. The
# blanket `*.wav` rules above therefore apply inside voices/ too.
#
# anne_vi.wav, anne_en.wav and reporter_vi.wav were committed before that
# decision and stay tracked; an ignore rule never untracks a file. To run TTS
# locally with any other character, copy its <slug>_<lang>.wav in by hand.
!voices/
